00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.290
one more thing, and he
introduced the iPhone?

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.680
What happened after that was the
peak of inflated expectations.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.220
The iPhone, the
cell phone was going

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.380
to do away with everything.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.180
We wouldn't need desktop
computers anymore.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.073
We wouldn't need laptop
computers anymore.

00:02:44.073 --> 00:02:46.365
All we would need is one of
these devices in our pocket

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:48.010
and it would do everything.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:50.113
And while those devices
were revolutionary

00:02:50.113 --> 00:02:52.530
and we all have smartphones
or most of us have smartphones

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.480
now, they didn't
replace the desktop.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.840
They didn't replace the laptop.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.500
We went through that peak
of inflated expectations.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.370
And then, once the
trough of disillusionment

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.430
hits, when people
